  "answer": "The higher-authority business evidence supports prioritizing **regulated mid-market and enterprise organizations**, not education startups. The quantitative segment analysis in [NL-016#NL-016-S03] shows mid-market (28 accounts) and enterprise (9 accounts) jointly generate 83.8% of recurring revenue, with enterprise churn at 1.3% and mid-market at 2.1%, compared to SMB churn at 4.8% and NPS of 31 versus 47 (mid-market) and 52 (enterprise). The same evidence explicitly overrides the prior sales playbook (NL-009) that highlighted education startups, stating metrics prove smaller startups (e.g., EduVantage Labs) show weak long-term retention. The CEO in [NL-015#NL-015-S03] confirms the ICP is regulated mid-market and enterprise (500–10,000 employees, heavy documentation), rejecting the SMB/education-startup pivot proposed by sales.\n\nThe trade-off is a **longer, more complex onboarding and sales cycle**: enterprise onboarding takes a median of 8.7 weeks due to permission and security complexities, and mid-market takes 5.2 weeks [NL-016#NL-016-S03]. This requires navigating extensive security reviews and more implementation resources, as highlighted in [NL-015#NL-015-S03] (\"Let's talk about how we can address the onboarding bottlenecks\").\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
